# Ephemeral fixture written by scripts/tests/local_ci_gate_set_e_test.sh to
# force a deliberate `cargo fmt --check` diff and prove the gate catches it.
# The test names it from mktemp and removes it on an EXIT trap, so it should
# never persist — but it has been swept into commits twice by `git add -A`
# running while the test was mid-flight (see the .VMoeOa.rs and .XXXXXX.rs
# paths in history). Ignoring it makes that impossible. Safe: the test uses
# git zero times and the gate mechanism is `cargo fmt --check`, which is
# git-agnostic.
infra/api/tests/_local_ci_set_e_regression_fixture.*.rs

# Generated by scripts/local-dev-up.sh so standalone `cd infra && cargo test`
# inherits the lane-local Flapjack source URL without a parent-shell export.
infra/.cargo/config.toml

# Suite artifact roots written by scripts/tests/apply_ses_log_read_policy_test.sh
# under the checkout root ($REPO_ROOT/.test_artifacts/<suite>_$$_$RANDOM). The
# suite removes them on an EXIT trap, but the trap does not run when the session
# is hard-killed — matt terminates a session after 300s of silent stdout — so a
# concurrent `git add -A` sweeps the residue into a commit. This is the same
# failure mode as the set-E fixture above and takes the same fix: 77 such files
# reached batman/jul28_6am_9_batch_union_close_and_ssot_reconcile that way.
# The paths are repo-relative on purpose (the suite proves the SUT's relative
# --artifact-dir handling and its sibling-preservation contract), so ignoring
# the root is the correct guard rather than relocating the suite to mktemp.
.test_artifacts/
